From 75558b1927fca545b99d48770a4b0da719c21116 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 09:29:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 089/202] phy: mediatek: mipi-dsi: Add MT6858 support

The MT6858 MIPI TX is close to the MT8196 one, but
with the bandgap controls at 0x0c, the PRD reference select at 0x10,
PLL_EN at bit 4 of PLL_CON1, the lane software-control registers 0x18
lower, and a PLL that runs at the full lane rate rather than half of
it. Sequence and values follow the vendor driver's MT6858 PLL
prepare/unprepare: bandgap core, then low-pass filter; lanes held in
software LP-11 while the SDM powers up and leaves isolation; PCW in 8.24
fixed point from the 26 MHz crystal; PLL enable, then the clock output
enable at 0x60. Lanes go to the DSI engine in power_on_signal.

The impedance calibration the bootloader leaves in place is not touched.
